This extension adds Tomb Raider (2013) modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]TR2013 Mod Manager will be installed automatically.[/summary]

The extension will automatically download and install the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/tombraider2013/mods/112]TR2013 Mod Manager[/url], which is used to install and enable/disable ".tiger patch" mods for the game.
[b][color=#ffe599]Some mods require a tool called [url=https://gamebanana.com/tools/6973]TexMod[/url], which only works when running the game in DirectX 9 mode. The user will receive a notification in Vortex asking if they want to download TexMod.[/color][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]TR Reboot Mod Manager installs to the game folder, recognised by a "trreboottools.modmanager.exe" file.[/*]
[*]TexMod mods with a "texmod.exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]TexMod Pack mods with a ".tpf" file install to the "TexMod" folder.[/*]
[*]Manager mods with a ".tr9dtp", ".tr9material", ".tr9modeldata", ".t9script", ".t9shaderlib", ".tr9sound" or one of 3 other file types install to the "Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[/list]

[b][size=3]To run the game in DirectX 9 mode:
[/size][/b]1. Start the Registry Editor by opening the Windows Start Menu and typing "regedit.exe", then press Enter.
2. Paste this into the regedit address bar: [code]HKEY_CURRENT_USER&#92;Software&#92;Crystal Dynamics&#92;Tomb Raider&#92;Graphics[/code]
3. Change value [code]RenderAPI[/code] datavalue to 9.

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Tomb Raider (2013) mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

TR Reboot Mod Manager:

Recognised when the archive contains a "trreboottools.modmanager.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

TexMod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "texmod.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

TexMod Pack:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".tpf" file.

  Installs to: "TexMod"

========================================================================

Manager Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".tr9dtp", ".tr9material", ".tr9modeldata", ".t9script", ".t9shaderlib", ".tr9sound", ".dds", ".tr9objectref", ".tr9dtp" or ".tr9anim" file.

  Installs to: "Mods"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

